---
const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What is Claude AI?',
    a: 'Claude is an AI assistant made by Anthropic — similar to ChatGPT but often sharper for writing, analysis, and domain-specific tasks. Skills and plugins are add-ons that make Claude significantly more capable for specific types of work.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I need a Claude subscription to use these bundles?',
    a: "Yes — you'll need a Claude Pro subscription ($20/month) to install and use skills and plugins. Think of Loadout as the setup that makes that $20 actually earn its keep for your job.",
  },
  {
    q: 'How long does setup take?',
    a: "Most buyers are up and running in under 30 minutes. Every bundle includes a step-by-step setup guide with screenshots. If you can copy and paste, you can do this.",
  },
  {
    q: 'Is there a guarantee?',
    a: "Yes. Every Loadout bundle comes with a 14-day no-questions-asked refund. If it doesn't work for you, email us and we'll sort it out.",
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I buy more than one bundle?',
    a: "Absolutely. Each bundle is priced individually, and they stack — you can have multiple niche setups running in the same Claude account.",
  },
];
---
<section class="py-28 px-5 sm:px-8 border-t border-edge">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">

    <div data-reveal class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-white mb-3">Questions</h2>
    </div>

    <dl class="space-y-0">
      {faqs.map((faq, i) => (
        <div
          data-reveal
          data-reveal-delay={String(Math.min(i + 1, 5))}
          class="border-t border-edge py-6"
        >
          <dt class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-2">{faq.q}</dt>
          <dd class="text-muted text-sm leading-relaxed">{faq.a}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
      <div class="border-t border-edge"></div>
    </dl>

  </div>
</section>
